WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.860
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.160
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.440
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.700
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.520
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为您制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:19.500
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉您的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:20.640
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.780
Hey, gang.
嘿，各位。

9
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.040
Hey, everybody.
嘿，大家好。

10
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.140
We are here this week to finish talking about Launch Party.
本周我们继续讨论《发布会》。

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.920
It's Launch Party Part 2.
这是《发布会》下集。

12
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.760
And it is a launch party of the Dunder Mifflin Infinity website.
这是关于“邓德·米夫林无限”网站的发布会。

13
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.980
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

14
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.420
Jinx.
真巧。

15
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.300
Buy me a Coke.
请我喝可乐。

16
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:49.740
It's Season 4, Episode 6, written by Jen Salata and directed by Ken Whittingham.
这是第四季第六集，由简·萨拉塔编剧，肯·惠廷汉执导。

17
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.420
Here is a summary.
这是剧情梗概。

18
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.580
Do it.
请讲。

19
00:00:52.960 --> 00:01:02.060
This week, Michael returns to Scranton after realizing he was not invited to the big New York launch party for Dunder Mifflin Infinity.
本周，迈克尔意识到自己没被邀请参加在纽约举办的“邓德·米夫林无限”盛大发布会，于是回到了斯克兰顿。

20
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.260
But instead, he has to celebrate via webcam.
但他只能通过网络摄像头参与庆祝。

21
00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:12.660
So he decides to ramp up the launch party in Scranton, and he gives Angela a very long list of demands.
所以他决定在斯克兰顿大办发布会，并给安吉拉列了一长串要求。

22
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.660
Then he orders pizza.
然后他点了披萨。

23
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:23.660
But when the pizza delivery guy refuses to honor Michael's half-off coupon, he holds him hostage in the conference room.
但当披萨外卖员拒绝接受迈克尔的半价优惠券时，他把对方扣押在会议室里。

24
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.420
Meanwhile, Andy tries to woo Angela to the dismay of Dwight.
与此同时，安迪试图追求安吉拉，这让德怀特感到沮丧。

25
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.660
Does he?
是吗？

26
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.800
He's relentless.
他锲而不舍。

27
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.400
And a little charming.
而且还有点迷人。

28
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.760
And a little charming.
而且还有点迷人。

29
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.040
And a little douchey.
还有点混蛋。

30
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.020
We'll get there.
我们待会儿再说这个。

31
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:38.980
All right.
好吧。

32
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.760
Fast fact number one.
第一个速览事实。

33
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.080
We have a big guest star alert.
我们要发布一个重磅客串明星预警。

34
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.620
Yes, we're so excited, you guys.
没错，大家伙儿，我们太激动了。

35
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.460
The pizza delivery guy was played by Kevin McHale.
披萨外卖员由凯文·麦克哈尔饰演。

36
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.900
Now, you guys probably know Kevin because he would go on to be a regular on the TV show Glee.
大家可能认识凯文，因为他后来成了电视剧《欢乐合唱团》的常驻演员。

37
00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:58.560
But this was about two years before that happened.
但这发生在那之前大约两年。

38
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.740
This appearance on The Office was one of his first television acting jobs.
他在《办公室》的这次客串是他最早的电视表演工作之一。

39
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.240
So we reached out to him to hear how it all went down.
所以我们联系了他，想听听当时的情况。

40
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.020
Yeah.
没错。

41
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.220
Kevin, thanks for letting me slide into your DMs.
凯文，谢谢你让我私信骚扰你。

42
00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.260
Angela really slid into his DMs, guys.
伙计们，安吉拉真的私信骚扰了他。

43
00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.420
Hey, I always feel so weird, but he's a very nice person.
嘿，我总是觉得很尴尬，但他是个非常好的人。

44
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.140
I was like, hey, Angela and Jenna here.
我当时说，嘿，我是安吉拉和珍娜。

45
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:18.420
Hello.
你好。

46
00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.700
And he was wonderful.
他真是太棒了。

47
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.660
He sent us an audio clips.
他给我们发来了音频片段。

48
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.800
And here is what he had to say, you guys, about coming in to audition for the role.
各位，这是他关于来试镜这个角色的讲述。

49
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.020
It's so charming.
太迷人了。

50
00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.300
Sam, can you play that clip?
萨姆，能播放一下那个片段吗？

51
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.900
So what I remember about the audition is actually the callback because the initial audition, no memory,
关于那次试镜，我真正记得的是复试，因为初试我完全没印象了，

52
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.960
but the callback, I was waiting in the stairwell.
但在复试时，我当时在楼梯间里等着。

53
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.400
It was me and Dave Franco and a couple other guys.
当时在那儿的还有戴夫·弗兰科和其他几个人。

54
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.380
And then one of the casting assistants comes out and says, oh, we're going to start in a few minutes,
然后一位选角助理出来说，哦，我们几分钟后就开始，

55
00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.620
but we just have to wait for Steve.
但我们得先等史蒂夫过来。

56
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.780
And I'm someone who has terrible, terrible nerves.
而我这人特别容易紧张，紧张得要命。

57
00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.580
And I don't know if my manager didn't know and didn't tell me,
我不知道是不是我的经纪人没意识到还是没告诉我，

58
00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.260
but I was very unaware that Steve Carell was going to read with us for the callback.
但我完全不知道史蒂夫·卡瑞尔会亲自来和我们对戏进行复试。

59
00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:13.880
And I went in, I sat there and tried with all my might just to get the words out.
我走进去坐下，拼尽全力才把台词说出来。

60
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:21.000
And at some point, Steve Carell chuckled, looked at the casting director, and they chuckled.
就在某个瞬间，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔轻笑了一声，看了看选角导演，他们都笑了。

61
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.880
And I was like, oh, my God, I made him laugh.
我当时心想，天哪，我把他逗笑了。

62
00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.120
And that was it.
就是这样。

63
00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.320
Like, if I didn't get the job, I was happy enough just with that,
就算我没得到这份工作，光是这一点我就足够开心了，

64
00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.420
that I made he and Alison Jones laugh.
因为我把他和艾莉森·琼斯都逗笑了。

65
00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.800
By the way, Alison Jones, the casting director,
顺便提一下，艾莉森·琼斯，那位选角导演，

66
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:39.760
she was the first casting director to just continuously give me a chance
她是第一位不断给我机会的选角导演，

67
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.900
when I hadn't worked or booked anything.
那时我还没什么工作经验，也没接到过什么戏。

68
00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.020
And she kept getting me further and further along in these jobs,
她不断让我进入这些工作的后续环节，

69
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.040
like this or super bad.
比如这部戏或者《太坏了》之类的。

70
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.500
And she just kept putting me in the room.
她就是一直让我去参加试镜。

71
00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.840
And I have her to thank for giving me any confidence
我得感谢她给了我信心，

72
00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.180
to even continue to pursue acting at all.
让我能够继续坚持演艺事业。

73
00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.680
Oh, that's Alison Jones.
哦，那就是艾莉森·琼斯。

74
00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:01.660
Yeah.
没错。

75
00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:06.120
And then also Steve, just so gracious coming there for those callbacks and
还有史蒂夫，他能亲自来参加那些复试真是太亲切了，

76
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.800
being there in the scene with him like that.
能那样和他一起演戏（感觉真好）。

77
00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.800
I mean, I just loved that story.
我是说，我真的很喜欢这个故事。

78
00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.140
But I see why they asked Steve to pop in on this audition,
但我明白他们为什么请史蒂夫来参加这次试镜了，

79
00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:19.000
because the pizza delivery guy, it's all him and Steve and Rain.
因为披萨外卖员那场戏，全是他、史蒂夫和雷恩的对手戏。

80
00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:19.420
Yeah.
没错。

81
00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.720
And Steve was a big star.
而且史蒂夫当时已经是大明星了。

82
00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.560
And the last thing you want to do is hire someone and bring them to set.
你最不想看到的就是雇了个人带到片场，

83
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.860
And then they freeze up because they're now performing,
结果他们因为现在面对的不是选角助理，

84
00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.960
not with a casting associate, but with this big star.
而是这位大明星，就紧张得僵住了。

85
00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.200
So he did it.
所以他做到了。

86
00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.100
He made it through and he got the job.
他挺过来了，并且拿到了那个角色。

87
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:36.760
Yeah.
没错。

88
00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.660
I like when he said,
我喜欢他说的那句，

89
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.160
I was just concentrating on getting the words out.
我当时只是专注于把台词说出来。

90
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.880
Well, he does a great, great job in this part.
嗯，他在这个角色里表现得非常、非常棒。

91
00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:46.540
And guys,
伙计们，

92
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:50.180
he sent in a few other audio clips that we'll sprinkle in throughout the episode.
他还发来了一些其他的音频片段，我们会在节目中穿插播放。

93
00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:50.860
Yeah.
没错。

94
00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:51.800
All right.
好的。

95
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.200
So what's your fast fact number two?
那么你的第二个速记事实是什么？

96
00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:53.980
Okay.
好的。

97
00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.260
My fast fact number two,
我的第二个速记事实是，

98
00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.580
and when I was researching this episode,
当我在研究这一集的时候，

99
00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.760
I was going through my archives and all this stuff started popping up
我翻阅了我的档案，然后所有这些东西都冒了出来，

100
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.400
from the 2007 Emmy Awards.
都是关于2007年艾美奖的。

101
00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:05.400
Yes.
是的。

102
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.100
Oh, that was a fun one.
噢，那集拍得真有意思。

103
00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:07.860
Yes.
没错。

104
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.820
We shot this episode right around the same time as the Emmys.
我们拍这一集的时候，正好赶上艾美奖颁奖礼前后。

105
00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.420
And this was the year that I was nominated.
那一年我正好被提名了。

106
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.560
I know it was a big deal.
我知道那可是件大事。

107
00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.920
We were so excited.
我们当时都兴奋极了。

108
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.580
It was so cool.
真是太酷了。

109
00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.240
And I found a blog that I wrote on MySpace about getting the nomination.
我还在MySpace上翻到了我当时写的一篇关于获得提名的博客。

110
00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.020
Oh.
噢。

111
00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.080
And it's so cute.
写得特别可爱。

112
00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:28.520
I got to hear the old,
我终于能听到那篇古老的、

113
00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:30.720
ye olde MySpace blog.
古老的MySpace博客了。

114
00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:31.820
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

115
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.240
Here's what I wrote.
我当时是这么写的。

116
00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.480
Man, I am so excited.
天哪，我太激动了。

117
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.200
I just can't tell you what this means to me.
我简直无法形容这对我的意义。

118
00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.060
Not because it is an award or something like that,
不是因为它是一个奖项之类的东西，

119
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.640
but because it feels like it's for our gal, Pam.
而是因为我觉得这像是为了我们的女孩，帕姆。

120
00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:47.700
She's a shy girl who doesn't get recognized very often, you know?
她是个害羞的女孩，平时不太受关注，你懂吧？

121
00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:54.820
It's like that shot from the episode with the art show where Pam is standing in front of her display waiting for the first visitor to come by.
就像艺术展那一集里的镜头，帕姆站在她的作品前，等着第一个参观者到来。

122
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.240
That just sums it all up for me.
那对我来说简直就是一切的缩影。

123
00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:05.620
So I guess I feel it in that part of me that is Pam, the part that still gets excited to show my art and know people are responding to it.
所以我猜，我内心深处那个帕姆的部分感受到了，那个依然会因为展示自己的艺术作品并知道有人回应而感到兴奋的部分。

124
00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.220
It's like, hey, people showed up to my art show.
就像是，嘿，有人来看我的艺术展了。

125
00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.260
Aw, that is so sweet, Jenna.
噢，珍娜，那真是太贴心了。

126
00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:14.620
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

127
00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.600
I remember I did not win the Emmy.
我记得我当时没拿到艾美奖。

128
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.780
And I remember thinking, like, damn it.
我记得当时心里想，该死。

129
00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.380
I wanted Pam to go up there and get her trophy.
我真希望帕姆能走上台去领她的奖杯。

130
00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.620
It was like her Dundies moment.
那就像是她的邓迪奖时刻。

131
00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:25.480
I know.
我知道。

132
00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.180
I really wanted to say I feel God in this Emmys tonight.
我当时真的好想说，我今晚在艾美奖感受到了上帝。

133
00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:29.100
I know.
我知道。

134
00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.460
You were so excited.
你当时太兴奋了。

135
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:32.020
You had your opening line.
你连开场白都准备好了。

136
00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:33.160
It was going to crush.
那绝对会轰动全场的。

137
00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:34.840
You would have crushed it.
你肯定会表现得非常棒。

138
00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.100
I would have crushed it.
我肯定会表现得非常棒。

139
00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.580
But lady, you were my plus one.
但亲爱的，你当时是我的女伴。

140
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:39.200
I know.
我知道。

141
00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.700
I was about to say, I remember this year because you had a really hot date.
我正想说，我记得那一年，因为你带了一个超级火辣的约会对象。

142
00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.240
It was me.
就是我。

143
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.220
We got to go together and it was a blaSt.
我们一起去了，玩得特别开心。

144
00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.400
But it was also, if you remember, Angela, it was in the round.
但安吉拉，如果你还记得的话，那次是环形舞台。

145
00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.000
I will never forget it.
我永远忘不了。

146
00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.400
It was so bizarre.
真是太离谱了。

147
00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:03.480
So, you know, normally the Emmys, it's like in a traditional type theater where you sit in theater style seating, right?
你知道，通常艾美奖是在那种传统的剧院里举行，座位也是剧院式的，对吧？

148
00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:05.200
One row in front of the other.
一排排坐在前面。

149
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.080
Well, this year, it's like the Television Academy decided to mix it up.
但那一年，电视学院决定搞点新花样。

150
00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.980
And they put the seats in a circle.
他们把座位排成了一个圆圈。

151
00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.440
And the stage in the middle, a big circle.
舞台在中间，是一个大圆圈。

152
00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.180
So, it was like theater in the round.
所以，就像是环形剧场一样。

153
00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.280
And, Jenna, I remember where we were seated.
而且，珍娜，我记得我们坐在哪儿。

154
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.820
Oh, I knew the minute we took our seats, I wasn't going to win.
噢，我一坐下就知道，我肯定没戏了。

155
00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:24.960
Oh, honey.
噢，亲爱的。

156
00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.920
We were in the back of the circle.
我们坐在圆圈的后方。

157
00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.640
So, we faced everyone's butt all night.
所以，我们整晚都对着别人的屁股。

158
00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.080
All night, we just saw real fancy people's asses.
整晚，我们看到的都是那些大人物的屁股。

159
00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.160
That's what we saw.
我们看到的就只有这些。

160
00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:43.580
And we kept thinking, at some point, are they going to turn around and face our section?
我们一直在想，他们什么时候才会转过身来面对我们这一区呢？

161
00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:44.380
No.
没有。

162
00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.620
Never once.
一次都没有。

163
00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:51.020
The entire thing was performed as if there were not people sitting behind the speaker.
整场表演就好像坐在演讲者身后的人根本不存在一样。

164
00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.520
It was so bizarre.
真是太离谱了。

165
00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:57.380
And, you know, sometimes someone who would win would, like, sort of glance over their shoulder like,
而且，你知道，有时候获奖的人会稍微回头瞥一眼，就像是，

166
00:07:57.480 --> 00:07:59.020
Hey, guys, how are you back there?
嘿，伙计们，你们在后面还好吗？

167
00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.060
And we would get so excited.
然后我们就会特别兴奋。

168
00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:01.620
We're like, We're good.
我们就像是，我们很好。

169
00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:02.000
We're good.
我们很好。

170
00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:02.300
Hi.
嗨。

171
00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:03.580
But, yeah.
不过，确实。

172
00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.780
It just was an evening of fancy TV butts.
那晚简直就是一场名流电视屁股秀。

173
00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:07.640
That's what...
这就是……

174
00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:07.780
Yeah.
是啊。

175
00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.100
It was very funny.
真的很好笑。

176
00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:14.320
But something else I noticed when I was seeing all these photos pop up from this time, Angela,
但安吉拉，当我看到这段时间冒出的这些照片时，我还注意到了另一件事，

177
00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.180
was that my back was still not healed at the time.
那就是当时我的背伤还没好。

178
00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:22.620
And there were a lot of restrictions on what I was allowed to wear and not wear.
我对能穿什么、不能穿什么有很多限制。

179
00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.180
I couldn't wear anything that was too tight on my ribcage, too tight on my waiSt.
我不能穿任何勒住胸腔或腰部太紧的衣服。

180
00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.820
And I could not wear high heels.
而且我不能穿高跟鞋。

181
00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:32.820
So, I have all these pictures of us on different red carpets.
所以，我有好多我们走不同红毯的照片。

182
00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:33.100
Yeah.
是啊。

183
00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:40.260
Going to the various, you know, pre-eminent events and things where I'm wearing these baggy dresses
去参加各种，你知道，那些重要的活动，我穿着宽松的裙子，

184
00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.700
and, like, bejeweled flip-flops.
还有，镶满珠宝的人字拖。

185
00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:43.780
Yes.
没错。

186
00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.020
Yes.
是的。

187
00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:49.400
And, I mean, I just felt like in that moment, you were like family for me.
而且，我是说，那一刻我觉得你就像我的家人一样。

188
00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.220
Because my sisters love a bejeweled flip-flop.
因为我的姐妹们就爱镶珠宝的人字拖。

189
00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.020
They love it.
她们超爱。

190
00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:54.640
Yeah.
是啊。

191
00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:59.780
I wore bejeweled flip-flops to the 2007 Emmy Awards.
我穿过镶珠宝的人字拖去参加2007年的艾美奖。

192
00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.640
And you got to look at people's butts.
而且你还能盯着别人的屁股看。

193
00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:02.840
There you go.
就是这样。

194
00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.140
It was a special time.
那真是一段特别的时光。

195
00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.440
I was really bummed you didn't win, though.
不过，你没获奖我真的很沮丧。

196
00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.620
And I have no poker face.
而且我根本藏不住情绪。

197
00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.700
It's like when Steve didn't win year after year.
就像史蒂夫年复一年没获奖的时候一样。

198
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.480
You know, it's a good thing the camera's not on me.
你知道，幸好摄像机没对着我。

199
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.560
Our whips away faSt.
我们的镜头很快就移开了。

200
00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.500
Because it's all across my face.
因为我的表情全写在脸上了。

201
00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:20.360
It's, what the?
这是，什么鬼？

202
00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:26.840
You know, they really missed an opportunity for some good television by not having the camera on you.
你知道吗，他们没把镜头对准你，真是错失了绝佳的电视效果。

203
00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.440
Every time one of us loSt.
每次我们输的时候。

204
00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:29.120
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

205
00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:32.480
That's before the day of, like, the memes.
那是在表情包还没流行起来的年代。

206
00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.360
My face would have been a meme.
我的脸肯定会被做成表情包。

207
00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:35.900
For sure.
绝对会。

208
00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.440
For sure.
肯定的。

209
00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.060
All right, lady.
好了，女士。

210
00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:44.020
Well, I'm going to move us on to fast fact number three because I've got a great big surprise for you.
好吧，我要带大家进入第三个速览事实了，因为我给你们准备了一个超级大惊喜。

211
00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:44.820
I know.
我知道。

212
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.980
You've been a little braggy about this in text to me leading up.
你在之前的短信里一直跟我吹嘘这个。

213
00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.060
She's like, mm-hmm, just wait for fast fact number three.
她就像是，嗯哼，等着瞧第三个速览事实吧。

214
00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:51.400
I'm like, okay.
我就说，好吧。

215
00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.740
What is it?
到底是什么？

216
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.920
I got the deep dive on Pam's plants.
我深入挖掘了帕姆的植物背后的故事。

217
00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.200
Shut up.
闭嘴。

218
00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:01.780
Shut up.
别开玩笑了。

219
00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:05.920
I know everything about Pam's plants and who's responsible for them.
关于帕姆的植物以及是谁在负责它们，我全都知道。

220
00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

221
00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.660
I have to tell you, I was texting with Jen Salata last night.
我得告诉你，昨晚我在和简·萨拉塔发短信。

222
00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:11.960
And Jen texted me.
简给我发短信说。

223
00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:18.360
She said, Ange, I didn't even know that Pam had a plant at front reception until I started listening to your podcaSt.
她说，安吉，在听你们的播客之前，我甚至都不知道前台接待处有帕姆的植物。

224
00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.880
I need to know all of this.
我必须知道这一切。

225
00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:21.940
What, what, what, what?
什么，什么，什么，什么？

226
00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:22.420
Tell me.
快告诉我。

227
00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.540
All right.
好的。

228
00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:26.440
I reached out to our set designer, Michael Gallenberg.
我联系了我们的布景设计师迈克尔·加伦伯格。

229
00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.060
Yes.
没错。

230
00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:30.000
Who told me it was Steve Ducharer.
他告诉我那是史蒂夫·杜查雷。

231
00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.080
The lead set dresser.
首席布景师。

232
00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:33.000
Yes.
是的。

233
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.620
Who was in charge of Pam's plants.
他负责帕姆的植物。

234
00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:41.060
I had a feeling it would be him because he sort of like set that whole area every day.
我当时就有预感是他，因为他每天都会布置那一整块区域。

235
00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:42.140
Yes.
是的。

236
00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:44.320
Well, I called Steve.
于是我给史蒂夫打了电话。

237
00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:45.000
You did?
你打了？

238
00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:45.480
Angela.
安吉拉。

239
00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:46.040
Yes.
是的。

240
00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.040
We had the best conversation.
我们聊得非常开心。

241
00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:48.820
Oh.
噢。

242
00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:55.580
So I remembered Steve mainly as the guy who was always having to deal with our computers.
我印象中史蒂夫主要是那个总是要处理我们电脑的人。

243
00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:56.560
Yes.
没错。

244
00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:57.200
He would come.
他会过来。

245
00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.780
And also like if our lamps went out or.
还有如果我们的台灯坏了或者什么的。

246
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:00.180
Yeah.
是啊。

247
00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.380
Sort of like all the things on our desk that needed attention.
基本上就是桌上所有需要维护的东西。

248
00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:04.240
Yeah.
没错。

249
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.040
Well, I told Steve that because he said, Jenna, do you remember me?
我把这些告诉了史蒂夫，因为他当时问我，珍娜，你还记得我吗？

250
00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.220
And I said, yes, Steve.
我说，记得，史蒂夫。

251
00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:14.280
My memory of you is that you were always crouching under my desk dealing with my computer.
我对你的印象就是你总是蹲在我的桌子底下摆弄我的电脑。

252
00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.920
And he laughed so hard.
他听了笑得特别大声。

253
00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:22.300
And he said, well, that was probably 80% of my job was just dealing with all of the computers at your desk.
他说，好吧，我大概80%的工作时间确实都花在处理你桌上的那些电脑上了。

254
00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:28.060
He said he was the one that was in charge of finally setting up the speaker on Oscar's desk.
他说他就是那个最终负责在奥斯卡的桌子上安装音箱的人。

255
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:28.740
You remember?
你还记得吗？

256
00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:29.260
Yes.
记得。

257
00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:29.480
Yeah.
是啊。

258
00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:30.200
All of that.
全都是那些事儿。

259
00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:31.840
So we really went down memory lane.
所以我们真的是好好回忆了一番往事。

260
00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:40.100
But he also told me that he was in charge of all of the items on our desk, including all of the plants in the office.
但他还告诉我，他负责我们桌上所有的东西，包括办公室里所有的植物。

261
00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:44.840
So here is what he told me about Pam's plants at reception.
所以，这是他告诉我的关于帕姆前台那些植物的事。

262
00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.320
Wait, did you tell him that I'm obsessed with them?
等等，你告诉他我对那些植物很着迷了吗？

263
00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:48.560
Yes.
说了。

264
00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:56.840
Because I had to explain why I was suddenly calling him to ask him multiple questions about the plants on the reception desk.
因为我得解释为什么我突然打电话给他，问他一堆关于前台植物的问题。

265
00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.140
I had to give some context.
我得给点背景信息。

266
00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.440
So he didn't think you were crazy.
这样他就不会觉得你疯了。

267
00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:00.220
No.
没。

268
00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.120
I mean, he might still think we're crazy.
我是说，他可能还是会觉得我们疯了。

269
00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.280
But I mean, he's like retired and living in Oregon now.
但他现在已经退休，住在俄勒冈州了。

270
00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:06.780
So.
所以。

271
00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:07.780
All right.
好吧。

272
00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:09.280
Here is what he told me, Ange.
安吉，这是他告诉我的。

273
00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:15.660
So you might remember, he had a little office on our stages that was behind Michael Scott's office.
你可能还记得，他在我们的摄影棚里有个小办公室，就在迈克尔·斯科特的办公室后面。

274
00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:16.040
Oh, yeah.
哦，记得。

275
00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:16.920
I remember it.
我有印象。

276
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:22.460
It was like a wooden, like they built him like a wooden kind of shed right there.
那就像个木头房子，他们就在那儿给他搭了个木头棚子一样。

277
00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:23.280
Yes.
对。

278
00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:30.540
And lining his walls were all kinds of tchotchkes and things that he would place all around the office.
他的墙上摆满了各种各样的装饰品，还有他会放在办公室各处的小玩意儿。

279
00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:31.100
Yes.
没错。

280
00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:43.760
So right outside of his office, he had a tiny like grow station and a plant care station for all of the plants in the office.
所以在他办公室外面，他有一个小小的培育站，还有一个专门照料办公室所有植物的护理站。

281
00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:54.940
He said for Pam's desk, he said for Pam's desk, he had only about three different plants and they were in plastic pots and he would rotate them randomly.
他说关于帕姆的桌子，他只有大约三种不同的植物，它们都种在塑料盆里，他会随机轮换它们。

282
00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:59.920
But he had an assortment, as we've noticed, of ceramic pots.
但正如我们注意到的，他有一堆陶瓷花盆。

283
00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.360
So that was how he kind of tried to make them look different.
所以这就是他试图让它们看起来不一样的方法。

284
00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:07.020
He said that it was absolutely, totally random.
他说这完全是随机的。

285
00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.800
What plant he put on the desk?
他把哪种植物放在桌上？

286
00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:21.580
Because I asked him about the flowering plant for beach games and if it was symbolic that Pam bloomed in that episode and he laughed and he said, no,
因为我问过他关于“海滩游戏”那一集里的开花植物，问那是不是象征着帕姆在那一集里绽放了，他笑了笑说，不，

287
00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.340
that's just a wonderful coincidence.
那只是一个美妙的巧合。

288
00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:36.080
He told me that Greg was very, very strict about the set decoration and that they were not allowed to change anything without Greg's permission.
他告诉我，格雷格对布景装饰非常非常严格，未经格雷格允许，他们不准改动任何东西。

289
00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:38.340
Tiny details, they would get in trouble.
哪怕是细小的细节，他们都会惹上麻烦。

290
00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:45.940
He said Greg never noticed the changing plants and he never consulted Greg about the plants.
他说格雷格从来没注意到植物的变化，他也从没就植物的事咨询过格雷格。

291
00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.780
It was his own little thing that he did each week.
这是他每周自己做的小动作。

292
00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:52.380
It was his own small act of rebellion that he would have different.
这是他小小的反叛行为，就是换上不同的植物。

293
00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:53.800
Different plants.
不同的植物。

294
00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:55.400
Yes.
是的。

295
00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.680
Well, Steve, I noticed.
好吧，史蒂夫，我注意到了。

296
00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.960
Angela noticed, Steve.
安吉拉注意到了，史蒂夫。

297
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:10.640
He said that he thinks he did a Christmas cactus once and that over the holiday episodes, he would always try to do something maybe a little different.
他说他记得有一次用了蟹爪兰，在节日特辑期间，他总是会尝试做点不一样的。

298
00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.940
But mostly it was just these little ferns.
但大部分时间都只是这些小蕨类植物。

299
00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:17.260
I will be looking for that Christmas cactus.
我会去找找那个蟹爪兰的。

300
00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:18.680
Oh, me too.
哦，我也是。

301
00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:19.840
I got so excited.
我太激动了。

302
00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.500
I was like, oh, I don't think we've seen that yet.
我当时心想，噢，我觉得我们还没见过那个呢。

303
00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:22.820
We haven't seen Christmas cactus.
我们还没见过圣诞仙人掌。

304
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.660
Everybody look out for Christmas cactus.
大家留意一下圣诞仙人掌。

305
00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:29.200
I'm going to have to go back to the Christmas episodes, but I do not remember a cactus.
我得回去重看一遍圣诞特辑，但我真不记得有仙人掌。

306
00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:31.880
Well, here's the other thing he told me, Angela.
好吧，安吉拉，他还跟我说了另一件事。

307
00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.700
He would have to water all those plants.
他得负责给所有那些植物浇水。

308
00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:42.700
And if we ever went on a week long hiatus, he would take all the plants off the set and he would put them under grow lights.
如果我们休假一周，他就会把片场所有的植物都搬走，放在生长灯下养着。

309
00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.400
And Tom Melby would come and water them on our breaks.
休息期间，汤姆·梅尔比会过来给它们浇水。

310
00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.260
I believe that, Tom Melby.
我相信，汤姆·梅尔比。

311
00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:49.640
I believe that.
我相信。

312
00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:50.460
That's so sweet.
太贴心了。

313
00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:58.760
I remember, Steve, he would walk over to accounting and water the plant that was on the file cabinets between accounting and reception.
我记得史蒂夫会走到会计部，给会计部和前台之间文件柜上的那盆植物浇水。

314
00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:00.600
And we would chit chat.
我们还会闲聊几句。

315
00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.520
Well, here's the other thing he told me.
好吧，他还跟我说了另一件事。

316
00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:03.120
What?
什么？

317
00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:04.560
Not plant related.
跟植物无关。

318
00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:12.440
Steve Ducharer was also in charge of all of the plaques around the office.
史蒂夫·杜查雷还负责办公室里所有的牌匾。

319
00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:16.960
He made all of them, including that one that trolled Kelly Cantley.
所有的牌匾都是他做的，包括那个用来恶搞凯莉·坎特利的牌子。

320
00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:18.280
No.
不会吧。

321
00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:19.160
Oh, yep.
噢，没错。

322
00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:28.080
He was also in charge of the whiteboard by accounting, and he said he was the one who wrote that Steve was robbed after the Emmys that one year.
他还负责会计部旁边的白板，他说那年艾美奖之后，写下“史蒂夫被抢了”的人就是他。

323
00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.900
Oh, I love it.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

324
00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.100
Steve, look at you.
史蒂夫，看看你。

325
00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.400
You're like over there mixing up plants.
你在那儿又是摆弄植物。

326
00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.480
You're writing secret messages on the message board.
又是往留言板上写秘密信息。

327
00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:48.160
He told me that this job was just his favorite, and it was wonderful, and we just talked about what a special thing we had.
他告诉我这份工作是他最喜欢的，非常棒，我们聊了聊我们拥有的这份特别的经历。

328
00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.620
And he retired when the show ended.
剧集结束时他就退休了。

329
00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.720
He was like, I don't think it's going to get better, and he retired.
他说，我觉得不会有比这更好的工作了，于是他就退休了。

330
00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.380
Steve, you're not wrong.
史蒂夫，你说得没错。

331
00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.080
You're not wrong.
你说得没错。

332
00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:02.680
We've worked on other shows, and we've had good experiences and things, but I have to say,
我们也参与过其他剧集，也有过不错的经历，但我不得不说，

333
00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:09.700
it'd be pretty amazing to be able to just write off in the sunset after a show like The Office because it was that special.
能在《办公室》这样的剧集结束后功成身退，真是太棒了，因为它就是那么特别。

334
00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:10.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

335
00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:20.540
Well, lady, you know you got me that Morgan Gassell watercolor of the Beasley's botanicals for Christmas, everybody.
对了，各位，你们知道安吉拉圣诞节送了我一幅摩根·加塞尔画的“比斯利植物”水彩画吗。

336
00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:21.900
Angela got me this.
安吉拉送给我的。

337
00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.240
Yes.
是的。

338
00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:24.740
I mean, I could not be more excited.
我是说，我简直不能更激动了。

339
00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:27.340
This is Jenna's Christmas present from me.
这是珍娜送给我的圣诞礼物。

340
00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.580
I got her.
我送给她的。

341
00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:29.980
Morgan, you're so talented.
摩根，你太有才了。

342
00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:35.180
You painted all of Pam's plants, and Morgan gave me the original.
你画了帕姆所有的植物，摩根把原稿送给了我。

343
00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:39.780
She also gave me a painting of all of Angela Martin's weird blouses.
她还送了我一幅画，画的是安吉拉·马丁所有那些奇怪的衬衫。

344
00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.580
Yes, I've seen that.
是的，我见过那幅画。

345
00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:47.320
Yes, and Jenna, and a coffee mug of Pam's botanicals.
是的，还有珍娜，以及一个印有帕姆植物图案的咖啡杯。

346
00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.020
Jenna.
珍娜。

347
00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:49.540
Amazing.
太棒了。

348
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:50.360
Amazing.
太棒了。

349
00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:57.460
Well, I sent a print of Beasley's botanicals to Steve as a thank you.
我给史蒂夫寄了一张“比斯利植物”的印刷版画作为感谢。

350
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.200
Oh, that is so sweet.
噢，那真是太贴心了。

351
00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:02.140
I thought the man in charge should have her print as well.
我觉得负责人也应该有一份她的打印件。

352
00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.060
Yes.
是的。

353
00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:04.480
Oh, I love that.
噢，我太喜欢这个了。

354
00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:11.840
He also sent me a photo of himself in his office on stage, and now that I've told you, I can send it to you.
他还给我发了一张他在舞台办公室里的照片，既然我已经告诉你们了，那我也能发给你们了。

355
00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.100
And guys, he said we can put it up on Office Ladies Pod as well.
伙计们，他说我们也可以把它发到《办公室女士》播客上。

356
00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:15.960
Oh, we will.
噢，我们会的。

357
00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:20.220
And we'll put up some of Morgan's stuff so you can see in our stories, and this was wonderful.
我们还会发布一些摩根的东西，这样你们就能在我们的快拍里看到了，这真是太棒了。

358
00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.040
I loved it.
我喜欢极了。

359
00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:31.860
And guys, if you want to get one, go over to Society6, it's the number six, and search for Beasley's botanicals, and it'll pop up, and you can get one yourself.
伙计们，如果你们想买一个，去Society6网站，就是数字6那个，搜索“比斯利的植物”，它就会弹出来，你们就能自己买一个了。

360
00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:38.460
Well, let's take a break, and then when we come back, we will really get into this episode.
好了，我们休息一下，回来之后，我们将深入探讨这一集。

361
00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:43.200
Michael is not going to react well to the pizza delivery.
迈克尔对披萨外送的反应可不会好。

362
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.320
Oh, no.
噢，不。

363
00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.820
It's not going to be good.
这可不会有好结果。

364
00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:57.320
All right.
好吧。

365
00:17:57.580 --> 00:18:07.280
We are back, everyone, and we are going to open this episode with Michael and Jim returning from their very short road trip where they got, I don't even think,
我们回来了，各位，这一集开场是迈克尔和吉姆从他们那趟极短的公路旅行中回来，我觉得他们甚至都没，

366
00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:13.940
outside of Scranton before realizing that they're not invited to the big New York party.
离开斯克兰顿，就意识到他们没被邀请参加纽约的大派对。

367
00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.340
So they come back, and Michael makes a big announcement.
所以他们回来了，迈克尔宣布了一个重大消息。

368
00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:19.900
Like, he actually wanted to be at the Scranton branch party.
就像，他其实是想参加斯克兰顿分公司的派对。

369
00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:21.700
He actually didn't want to go to New York, right?
他其实根本不想去纽约，对吧？

370
00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:22.760
Yes.
是的。

371
00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:26.040
And Stanley's like, wait, so we're not going home early?
斯坦利就说，等等，所以我们不能早点回家了？

372
00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:27.880
Yeah.
是啊。

373
00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.640
Michael's like, no, no.
迈克尔说，不，不。

374
00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:42.520
In fact, Michael calls Angela into his office, and he says to Angela, I want this party to be sexier, cooler, and more important than the one in New York.
事实上，迈克尔把安吉拉叫进办公室，对她说，我要让这个派对比纽约的那个更性感、更酷、更重要。

375
00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.840
And he gives her a list of demands.
然后他给了她一份要求清单。

376
00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:46.180
Yeah.
是啊。

377
00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.560
Let's just talk about this list for a minute, okay?
我们来聊聊这份清单吧，好吗？

378
00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:53.100
Now, remember, the party starts in one hour.
记住，派对一小时后就开始了。

379
00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:53.640
Yeah.
是啊。

380
00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.580
This is the liSt.
这就是那份清单。

381
00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:54.880
Ready?
准备好了吗？

382
00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:07.200
Beer, light beer, streamers, orchids, better lighting, something made of ice, pizza, pizza with mushrooms, pizza without mushrooms, white pizza, steak, chocolates, someone famous,
啤酒、淡啤酒、彩带、兰花、更好的照明、冰雕、披萨、蘑菇披萨、无蘑菇披萨、白披萨、牛排、巧克力、名人，

383
00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:11.400
cool music, confetti, go-go dancers, maybe Al Roker.
酷炫的音乐、五彩纸屑、舞女，也许还有阿尔·罗克。

384
00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:12.260
Yeah.
是啊。

385
00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:13.120
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

386
00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:17.740
Michael says he'll get the pizza since Angela's going to do all those other things in one hour.
迈克尔说他去买披萨，因为安吉拉要在这一小时内搞定所有其他事情。

387
00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:18.480
Yeah.
是啊。

388
00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:24.540
I mean, he wants the people in New York to be jealous that they got Al Roker to attend in Scranton.
我是说，他想让纽约的人嫉妒，因为他们能在斯克兰顿请到阿尔·罗克出席。

389
00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.720
How is that so hard to understand, Angela?
这有什么难理解的吗，安吉拉？

390
00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:27.540
I don't know.
我不知道。

391
00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:30.020
Just go get some go-go dancers and some steak.
赶紧去弄些舞女和牛排来。

392
00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.260
Possibly change the whole lighting scheme of the office.
顺便把办公室的整个照明方案改一下。

393
00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:34.060
That'd be great.
那太棒了。

394
00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:34.520
Thanks.
谢谢。

395
00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.500
But he tells Angela, if anyone can do it, it's you.
但他告诉安吉拉，如果有人能做到，那一定是你。

396
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:41.820
But actually, if there is someone who could do it better, could you let them know?
但实际上，如果有人能做得更好，你能告诉他们吗？

397
00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.240
What was it like for you to do that scene with Steve?
和你与史蒂夫演那场戏是什么感觉？

398
00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.700
Were you improvising any of the things on that list as you were reading them off?
你在读清单的时候，有没有即兴发挥其中的内容？

399
00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.160
Or was that pretty much scripted?
还是说基本上都是照着剧本演的？

400
00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:52.900
No, that was pretty much scripted.
不，那基本上都是照着剧本演的。

401
00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.080
And it was really fun because Steve has to interrupt me.
那真的很有趣，因为史蒂夫不得不打断我。

402
00:19:56.460 --> 00:20:00.020
And I just loved, loved doing scenes with him.
我真的非常、非常喜欢和他演对手戏。

403
00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:05.240
It felt like I got to be like in this comedic dance, you know?
感觉就像是在进行一场喜剧舞蹈，你懂吗？

404
00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:08.820
And except I'm dancing with like the best comedian in town.
只不过我的舞伴是城里最棒的喜剧演员。

405
00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:10.540
It just was so fun.
真的太好玩了。

406
00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.120
I was like, you know how you have like a body buzz, you know?
就像……你知道那种身体兴奋的感觉吗？

407
00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:18.540
Like I had that kind of feeling going in there to get to do scenes with him.
我每次去和他演对手戏时，都有那种感觉。

408
00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:21.280
And I loved every single second.
我享受其中的每一秒。

409
00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:23.560
And he would like, he would be so generous.
而且他真的非常慷慨。

410
00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:25.500
We've talked about this, but he'd let me have a moment.
我们聊过这个，他会留给我发挥的空间。

411
00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.460
Like when I say steak and I look at him, you know?
比如当我提到牛排并看向他时，你懂吗？

412
00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.640
Like he just let all of that breathe.
他会给这些表演留出呼吸的空间。

413
00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.280
I know exactly that body buzz you're talking about because I would get that feeling every
我完全明白你说的那种身体兴奋感，因为我每次拿到剧本，看到有帕姆和迈克尔的戏份时，

414
00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:38.260
time I'd get a script and be like, oh, there's a Pam Michael scene.
我都会有那种感觉。

415
00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.920
I get Steve all to myself.
我可以独享史蒂夫了。

416
00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:40.660
Yeah.
没错。

417
00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:42.440
And he's just so good.
他真的太棒了。

418
00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:47.100
And I feel like every person in a scene with Steve, Steve makes that person better.
我觉得和史蒂夫演对手戏的每一个人，都会因为他而变得更好。

419
00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:47.920
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

420
00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.680
Well, I love that scene.
我超爱那场戏。

421
00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:51.240
I watched it.
我看了。

422
00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:57.100
I rewound it and watched it a second time just because it was so, so delightful.
我还倒回去看了第二遍，因为它实在太、太令人愉悦了。

423
00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:58.000
Yes.
是的。

424
00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.820
And I had to memorize that list, guys.
而且伙计们，我得把那张清单背下来。

425
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.760
I'm not reading off.
我不是在照着念。

426
00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:01.980
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

427
00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.820
That wasn't written on the piece of paper for you?
那张纸上没给你写吗？

428
00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:04.460
No.
没有。

429
00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:09.060
I mean, you know, like I maybe the prop department had a list, but I had to learn that.
我是说，道具组可能有一份清单，但我必须得背下来。

430
00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:13.800
Well, and it's important because some of those elements are going to come up later, right?
嗯，这很重要，因为其中一些要素稍后会用到，对吧？

431
00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:16.360
So you had to make sure you said certain things.
所以你必须确保说出特定的内容。

432
00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:16.820
Yeah.
是的。

433
00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:24.780
Well, next up, Andy is trying to talk to Dwight to see what does he think about Angela?
接下来，安迪试图找德怀特谈谈，看看他是怎么看安吉拉的？

434
00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.560
Does he think that Andy should go after Angela?
他觉得安迪应该去追求安吉拉吗？

435
00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:29.640
And Dwight is like, no.
而德怀特的反应是，不行。

436
00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:37.160
Well, the first thing he says, which if you speak Dwight, you know, is one of the highest
他说的第一句话，如果你懂德怀特的语言，就知道这是他能给出的最高评价之一。

437
00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:38.860
compliments he could give anyone.
他说她很有效率。

438
00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:41.240
He says she's efficient.
那简直就像是直接往德怀特心口捅了一刀。

439
00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:47.400
Well, that's just like, that's like stabbing Dwight in the heart right there.
没错。

440
00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:48.080
Yeah.
他失去了这样一位高效的女性。

441
00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.400
That he's lost such an efficient woman.
是的。

442
00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:50.960
Yeah.
而且，你知道，德怀特显然不想让安迪去追求安吉拉。

443
00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:55.800
And, you know, Dwight does not obviously want Andy to make a play for Angela.
所以他告诉安迪，在办公室谈恋爱是不合适的。

444
00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:58.880
So he tells her it's inappropriate to date someone at work.
他还说安迪其实可以去追凯莉，因为她在附楼。

445
00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.660
And he could actually date Kelly because she's in the annex.
就像他可以追凯莉或者托比，但不能追他们办公区里的任何人。

446
00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:07.800
Like he can date Kelly or Toby, but not anyone in their immediate bullpen.
没错。

447
00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:08.300
Yeah.
好了，现在迈克尔得意洋洋地宣布，他订了大家最爱的那家店的披萨。

448
00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:15.040
Well, now Michael triumphantly announces that he has ordered pizza from everybody's favorite
大家起初还有点兴奋，直到他们发现迈克尔订错了披萨店。

449
00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:15.480
place.
那真的很有趣，因为史蒂夫不得不打断我。

450
