587
00:29:31.980 --> 00:29:36.320
Well, next up, Angela, we have this scene and I have some things to ask you about.
好了，接下来，安吉拉，我们有这一幕，我有些问题想问你。

588
00:29:37.460 --> 00:29:44.580
Andy is attempting to ask Angela out, but she is searching through this box of party supplies.
安迪试图约安吉拉出去，但她正在翻找那个派对用品盒。

589
00:29:44.780 --> 00:29:46.260
What do you think you're going to find in there?
你觉得你在里面能找到什么？

590
00:29:46.540 --> 00:29:48.320
What are you looking for in this box?
你在盒子里找什么呢？

591
00:29:48.500 --> 00:29:49.080
A steak?
牛排吗？

592
00:29:49.260 --> 00:29:50.360
An ice sculpture?
冰雕吗？

593
00:29:50.820 --> 00:29:53.440
You think any of the things on Michael's list better lighting?
你觉得迈克尔清单上的那些东西里，有更好的照明吗？

594
00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:55.080
It's a small box.
那只是个小盒子。

595
00:29:55.800 --> 00:29:57.880
It's a busy work box, Jenna.
那是个装忙碌工作的盒子，珍娜。

596
00:29:58.280 --> 00:30:02.140
It's a box so I could look busy and I could ignore Andy.
那是个让我看起来很忙，好让我能无视安迪的盒子。

597
00:30:03.220 --> 00:30:08.600
And what I gave to myself was like, clearly, I'm looking for more of those weird blue spiral
我给自己设定的心理活动是，很明显，我在找更多那种奇怪的蓝色螺旋

598
00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:11.240
thingies that I'm going to hang in the conference room later.
小玩意儿，我稍后要挂在会议室里。

599
00:30:12.400 --> 00:30:17.400
She had a vision of blue spiral thingies and she needed more of them.
她脑子里构想了蓝色螺旋小玩意儿，她需要更多这种东西。

600
00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:19.180
And so she's digging and digging.
所以她一直在翻找。

601
00:30:19.420 --> 00:30:22.400
But who uses this as a pickup line?
但谁会把这当成搭讪台词啊？

602
00:30:22.600 --> 00:30:26.820
Who thinks that a woman is going to like stop everything she's doing in your and just be like,
谁会觉得女人会停下手里的一切，然后对你说，

603
00:30:26.940 --> 00:30:27.380
you're right.
你说得对。

604
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:30.200
There's not dinner and a movie in this box.
这个盒子里可没有晚餐和电影。

605
00:30:31.580 --> 00:30:36.040
Well, lady, we also have a fan catch here from Abby Tilford.
好了，女士，我们这里还有一条来自Abby Tilford的粉丝发现。

606
00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:36.660
Okay.
好的。

607
00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:42.500
She says, in launch party, around 16 minutes, 25 seconds.
她说，在《发布会》那一集，大约16分25秒的时候。

608
00:30:42.800 --> 00:30:45.060
So this was a moment from last week's breakdown.
这是上周解析里的一个片段。

609
00:30:45.780 --> 00:30:48.600
Angela says she's been working on the party for two weeks.
安吉拉说她为了这个派对已经筹备两周了。

610
00:30:49.360 --> 00:30:55.280
But now at 25 minutes, 21 seconds, she says she's been planning it for three weeks.
但到了25分21秒，她又说她已经筹备三周了。

611
00:30:56.380 --> 00:30:58.920
Is this just Angela being dramatic?
这只是安吉拉在演戏吗？

612
00:30:58.920 --> 00:30:59.540
What is this?
这是怎么回事？

613
00:30:59.540 --> 00:31:01.080
This is a bit of a continuity catch.
这是一个连贯性上的小漏洞。

614
00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:02.020
And I looked.
我查了一下。

615
00:31:02.160 --> 00:31:02.700
She's right.
她是正确的。

616
00:31:02.980 --> 00:31:04.120
Oh, no, she's right.
噢，不，她是正确的。

617
00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:05.260
It's a continuity error.
这是一个连贯性错误。

618
00:31:05.260 --> 00:31:09.820
And maybe we can justify it by saying that Angela feels very put upon all of a sudden.
也许我们可以解释为安吉拉突然觉得压力很大。

619
00:31:10.140 --> 00:31:11.740
So maybe she's exaggerating.
所以她可能是在夸大其词。

620
00:31:11.920 --> 00:31:13.940
And I have an improv catch.
我还有一个即兴发挥的发现。

621
00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:17.020
I improvised the last line as I walked away.
我走开时即兴说了最后一句台词。

622
00:31:17.200 --> 00:31:20.120
I said, and Kevin had Greek food for lunch again.
我说，凯文午饭又吃了希腊菜。

623
00:31:20.280 --> 00:31:21.420
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

624
00:31:21.560 --> 00:31:22.300
That was an improv?
那是即兴发挥的？

625
00:31:22.820 --> 00:31:23.380
Yes.
是的。

626
00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:24.800
That was an improv.
那是即兴发挥的。

627
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:29.880
And what you don't see is that Matt Soane cut over to Brian as Kevin.
你没看到的是，Matt Soane切到了布莱恩饰演的凯文的镜头。

628
00:31:30.040 --> 00:31:31.080
And he was like, hey.
他当时就像是，嘿。

629
00:31:31.780 --> 00:31:41.250
I love that your character's go-to is always to find some subtle way to insult Kevin.
我喜欢你这个角色总是想方设法去含蓄地羞辱凯文。

630
00:31:41.590 --> 00:31:42.250
Yeah, of course.
是啊，当然。

631
00:31:42.250 --> 00:31:44.530
Because he has a constant annoyance for her.
因为他总是让她感到厌烦。

632
00:31:44.730 --> 00:31:45.250
Constant.
一直都是。

633
00:31:45.350 --> 00:31:46.470
All day long.
整天都是。

634
00:31:46.650 --> 00:31:49.570
I'm telling you, I think she requested the glass partition.
我跟你说，我觉得那个玻璃隔断是她要求的。

635
00:31:50.290 --> 00:31:51.670
He drives her crazy.
他快把她逼疯了。

636
00:31:51.870 --> 00:31:52.750
She needed a barrier.
她需要一道屏障。

637
00:31:53.810 --> 00:31:56.710
Well, now we have a little bit of Pam sass coming up.
好了，接下来是帕姆的毒舌时刻。

638
00:31:56.890 --> 00:31:58.370
The pizza guy has arrived.
送披萨的人到了。

639
00:31:58.610 --> 00:32:02.330
And Pam calls Michael and says, hey, the pizza by Alfredo guy is here.
帕姆给迈克尔打电话说，嘿，阿尔弗雷多披萨店的人来了。

640
00:32:02.710 --> 00:32:04.630
Michael says, you don't have to say it like that.
迈克尔说，你没必要那样说。

641
00:32:04.790 --> 00:32:06.570
And Pam says, I said it normal.
帕姆说，我说话很正常啊。

642
00:32:07.530 --> 00:32:09.170
I did say it normal.
我确实说得很正常。

643
00:32:09.570 --> 00:32:10.270
I know.
我知道。

644
00:32:10.410 --> 00:32:12.750
But I just love that Pam, this is this new.
但我就是喜欢帕姆这一点，这是全新的她。

645
00:32:12.890 --> 00:32:13.890
I'm in love, Pam.
我恋爱了，帕姆。

646
00:32:14.110 --> 00:32:15.110
I give zero Fs.
我完全不在乎。

647
00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:16.170
I say what I think.
我想到什么就说什么。

648
00:32:16.570 --> 00:32:17.650
And I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

649
00:32:17.650 --> 00:32:20.170
But yes, the pizza guy is here.
但没错，送披萨的人到了。

650
00:32:20.630 --> 00:32:25.210
And oh, man, this starts a whole Michael spiral.
天哪，这开启了迈克尔的一连串失控。

651
00:32:25.550 --> 00:32:30.830
Everything he is feeling about Ryan and feeling left out and not treated fairly,
他因为瑞安的事感到被冷落、觉得没受到公平对待，

652
00:32:30.830 --> 00:32:37.790
he is going to pile on this poor teenager who's just a pizza delivery guy.
于是他要把这些情绪发泄在这个可怜的青少年身上，人家只是个送披萨的。

653
00:32:38.050 --> 00:32:38.730
Yeah.
没错。

654
00:32:38.850 --> 00:32:45.070
He is mad because the pizza kid will not accept his half-off coupon for all of the pizzas.
他很生气，因为送披萨的小哥不接受他那张针对所有披萨的半价优惠券。

655
00:32:46.030 --> 00:32:50.310
He explains, you can have half-off two pizzas, but not all of the pizzas.
他解释说，优惠券上写的是两份披萨半价，而不是所有披萨都半价。

656
00:32:50.510 --> 00:32:53.610
And Michael is like, it doesn't say that anywhere on the coupon.
迈克尔却说，优惠券上根本没写那条规定。

657
00:32:54.070 --> 00:32:56.710
And the pizza kid is like, I don't know what to tell you.
披萨小哥则说，我也不知道该怎么跟你解释。

658
00:32:57.050 --> 00:33:01.110
I mean, he's basically like, if I give you half-off all these pizzas and I go back,
我的意思是，他基本上是在说，如果我给你这些披萨都打半价，我回去之后，

659
00:33:01.210 --> 00:33:01.930
I'm going to get in trouble.
我会惹上麻烦的。

660
00:33:02.250 --> 00:33:05.350
This is not, I mean, it's not my decision to make.
这真的不是，我是说，这事儿我说了不算。

661
00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:09.830
I can't authorize your new use of this coupon.
我没法批准你这种新的优惠券用法。

662
00:33:09.830 --> 00:33:15.490
Well, and listen, the pizza guy does have a little bit of that teenage sass, though,
嗯，听着，这披萨小哥确实带点青少年的那种傲慢，

663
00:33:15.770 --> 00:33:17.570
because he's like, not my problem.
因为他一副“这又不是我的问题”的态度。

664
00:33:17.930 --> 00:33:20.310
A little bit full teenager sass.
确实有点青少年的傲慢劲儿。

665
00:33:20.650 --> 00:33:22.910
Listen, this truly isn't his problem.
听着，这真的不是他的问题。

666
00:33:22.910 --> 00:33:24.590
And Michael needs to lighten up.
迈克尔真的该放轻松点。

667
00:33:24.750 --> 00:33:28.150
But the kid is also kind of an ass.
但那孩子也确实有点混蛋。

668
00:33:28.570 --> 00:33:29.430
For sure.
确实。

669
00:33:29.770 --> 00:33:35.750
Well, Michael's response to this is to have Dwight lock him in the conference room
嗯，迈克尔对此的反应是让德怀特把他锁在会议室里，

670
00:33:35.750 --> 00:33:38.610
until he decides to honor the coupon.
直到他决定接受那张优惠券为止。

671
00:33:38.610 --> 00:33:40.310
It's so irrational.
这太不理智了。

672
00:33:40.610 --> 00:33:45.570
He says that he needs to learn about respect and accountability and follow through.
他说那孩子需要学习什么是尊重、责任感和执行力。

673
00:33:45.790 --> 00:33:47.270
He's saying all this crazy stuff.
他一直在说这些疯话。

674
00:33:47.430 --> 00:33:49.570
And then, of course, he really loses it.
然后，当然，他彻底失控了。

675
00:33:49.690 --> 00:33:52.710
And it's like, the guy is like, this is stupid.
那感觉就像是，那小哥说，这太蠢了。

676
00:33:52.850 --> 00:33:55.150
And he's like, you don't even know what stupid is.
迈克尔就说，你根本不知道什么叫蠢。

677
00:33:55.330 --> 00:33:57.730
It's about to get all stupid up in here.
这里马上就要变得更蠢了。

678
00:33:58.310 --> 00:34:00.650
This is such an outrageous storyline.
这剧情真是太离谱了。

679
00:34:00.650 --> 00:34:03.790
As I was watching this episode, I just kept thinking,
我在看这一集的时候，一直在想，

680
00:34:03.790 --> 00:34:06.750
I can't believe we are doing this storyline.
真不敢相信我们竟然拍了这段剧情。

681
00:34:07.230 --> 00:34:08.490
It is so funny.
这太搞笑了。

682
00:34:08.910 --> 00:34:10.390
It is really broad.
这真的很夸张。

683
00:34:10.450 --> 00:34:11.470
It's really broad.
真的很夸张。

684
00:34:11.590 --> 00:34:15.470
But yet, at the same time, you kind of believe that Michael would do it.
但同时，你又觉得迈克尔确实干得出这种事。

685
00:34:15.610 --> 00:34:18.270
That Michael would be like, no, you're going to stay here and you're going to learn a lesson.
迈克尔会觉得，不，你得留在这儿，你得给我上一课。

686
00:34:18.490 --> 00:34:22.350
And everyone around him is like, you have just kidnapped someone.
而他周围的人都在说，你这简直是绑架了别人。

687
00:34:22.610 --> 00:34:24.970
You are currently holding someone hostage.
你现在是在扣押人质。

688
00:34:24.990 --> 00:34:25.950
And he's like, no, no, no.
他却说，不，不，不。

689
00:34:26.070 --> 00:34:27.070
I'm teaching him a lesson.
我是在教他做人的道理。

690
00:34:27.070 --> 00:34:40.190
Well, yeah, Kevin, Oscar, Stanley, they have all started researching kidnapping and accomplices to see if they can be charged as accessories to Michael's crime.
嗯，没错，凯文、奥斯卡、斯坦利，他们都开始研究绑架罪和从犯的相关法律，看看他们会不会因为迈克尔的罪行被控为共犯。

691
00:34:40.190 --> 00:34:42.390
But this is what Michael does.
但这正是迈克尔的行事风格。

692
00:34:42.710 --> 00:34:51.450
You know, it's like in the episode when he drives his car in the lake, he takes it out on the guy who ate the turtles from the gift basket.
你知道，就像他在那一集里把车开进湖里一样，他把气撒在了那个吃了礼品篮里乌龟的人身上。

693
00:34:52.430 --> 00:34:56.690
He always, like, shifts the blame and responsibility.
他总是这样，推卸责任和过错。

694
00:34:56.690 --> 00:35:03.110
If Michael is embarrassed or if Michael is upset about something, he takes it out on a very ordinary moment.
如果迈克尔感到尴尬或者因为某事心烦，他就会把气撒在一个非常普通的时刻上。

695
00:35:03.110 --> 00:35:04.330
And it's so funny.
这太搞笑了。

696
00:35:05.510 --> 00:35:08.050
And we've all sort of been there, right?
我们都有过这种经历，对吧？

697
00:35:08.170 --> 00:35:10.250
We've all had that displaced anger.
我们都曾有过那种迁怒于人的经历。

698
00:35:10.870 --> 00:35:16.690
Like, I'll never forget one time my dad had, he had ordered this new barbecue grill.
比如，我永远忘不了有一次我爸订了一个新的烧烤架。

699
00:35:16.910 --> 00:35:20.910
And Jenna, this guy in my hometown makes them, you know, like a smoker.
珍娜，我老家有个家伙专门做这种东西，你知道，就是那种熏烤炉。

700
00:35:21.110 --> 00:35:22.030
And he's a welder.
他是个焊工。

701
00:35:22.210 --> 00:35:24.510
And he made my dad this smoker.
他为我爸做了一个熏烤炉。

702
00:35:24.890 --> 00:35:27.850
And it took him a while because he makes it, you know, by hand.
他花了不少时间，因为你知道，那是他手工制作的。

703
00:35:27.850 --> 00:35:28.890
He's out there welding.
他在外面焊接。

704
00:35:28.890 --> 00:35:36.990
And my dad went to get it and he got a flatbed trailer to put it on and pull it behind our truck.
我爸去取它，还弄了一辆平板拖车，打算把它装上去，挂在我们的卡车后面拉回来。

705
00:35:37.170 --> 00:35:38.570
He was so excited.
他当时特别兴奋。

706
00:35:39.030 --> 00:35:40.590
We'd waited so long.
我们等了太久了。

707
00:35:40.730 --> 00:35:44.190
And he's driving down the driveway with it.
他正开着车把它拉进车道。

708
00:35:44.590 --> 00:35:52.610
And he didn't, like, factor in, like, the overhang of the carport and dented in the new smoker.
结果他没考虑到车棚顶部的突出部分，把新熏烤炉给撞瘪了。

709
00:35:52.870 --> 00:35:53.590
Oh, no.
噢，不。

710
00:35:53.910 --> 00:35:54.070
Yeah.
是啊。

711
00:35:54.330 --> 00:35:58.330
And for whatever reason, he kind of, we were all like, don't say anything.
不知怎么的，他当时那样子，我们都心照不宣地想：别说话。

712
00:35:58.330 --> 00:35:58.930
Don't say anything.
什么都别说。

713
00:35:59.270 --> 00:36:04.030
He got out of the car and he was like, if that tree hadn't been there, then he was,
他从车里出来，说要是那棵树没在那儿的话，然后他，

714
00:36:04.090 --> 00:36:05.270
like, going to cut down the tree.
就打算把那棵树砍了。

715
00:36:05.470 --> 00:36:07.790
And my mom was like, it's not the tree's fault.
我妈就说，这又不是树的错。

716
00:36:08.070 --> 00:36:10.290
It's part of it.
这很正常。

717
00:36:10.390 --> 00:36:14.870
You know, but we've all had these moments where we're so, like, upset and irrationally.
你知道，我们都有过这种时刻，当时特别心烦，甚至有些不理智。

718
00:36:15.010 --> 00:36:16.190
We're like, that's it.
我们就会觉得，就是它了。

719
00:36:16.690 --> 00:36:17.550
It's the tree.
都是那棵树的错。

720
00:36:18.450 --> 00:36:19.330
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

721
00:36:19.430 --> 00:36:22.210
Well, speaking of tree, that happened to me this year, Angela.
说到树，安吉拉，我今年也遇到了类似的事。

722
00:36:22.730 --> 00:36:25.310
We were all set to get our Christmas tree.
我们本来准备好要去买圣诞树了。

723
00:36:25.630 --> 00:36:25.830
Yeah.
嗯。

724
00:36:25.990 --> 00:36:28.550
On this one day, we were going to set up the Christmas tree.
就在那一天，我们打算把圣诞树支起来。

725
00:36:28.550 --> 00:36:30.790
And I can't remember what happened.
我不记得发生了什么。

726
00:36:31.050 --> 00:36:32.670
It was, like, something.
反正就是出了点事。

727
00:36:32.670 --> 00:36:33.930
And it was the night before.
那是前一天晚上。

728
00:36:34.170 --> 00:36:37.850
And I said to Lee, I said, so we're getting up early in the morning.
我对李说，我说，我们明天一早就要起床。

729
00:36:37.950 --> 00:36:38.870
We're going to go get our tree.
我们要去买树。

730
00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:40.290
We're going to decorate the tree tomorrow.
我们明天就要装饰那棵树。

731
00:36:40.530 --> 00:36:43.230
And he said very casually, well, I don't know.
他非常随意地说，嗯，我不知道。

732
00:36:43.330 --> 00:36:44.950
I mean, tomorrow or another day.
我是说，明天或者改天吧。

733
00:36:45.710 --> 00:36:48.110
And I was like, what?
我当时就想，什么？

734
00:36:48.870 --> 00:36:52.350
It's going to be tomorrow at 9 a.m.?
不是说好明天早上九点吗？

735
00:36:52.350 --> 00:36:55.030
And I, like, I was, like, a mess.
我当时整个人都崩溃了。

736
00:36:55.190 --> 00:36:57.090
