00:52:16.110 --> 00:52:17.650
No unsolicited pics.
别发不请自来的照片。

1044
00:52:18.090 --> 00:52:18.970
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1045
00:52:18.970 --> 00:52:20.230
Who's asking for pictures?
谁会要照片啊？

1046
00:52:20.430 --> 00:52:22.050
Now you put that in their brain.
现在你把这个念头植入他们脑子里了。

1047
00:52:23.880 --> 00:52:25.160
Pictures of what?
什么照片？

1048
00:52:25.800 --> 00:52:26.500
Their night.
他们当晚的照片。

1049
00:52:27.060 --> 00:52:28.200
That's inappropriate.
那太不合适了。

1050
00:52:28.780 --> 00:52:30.900
That's why I'm saying don't send them.
所以我才说别发。

1051
00:52:31.260 --> 00:52:32.460
I don't want photos.
我不要照片。

1052
00:52:32.640 --> 00:52:33.680
I don't want details.
我不要细节。

1053
00:52:33.980 --> 00:52:34.620
Just tell me.
直接告诉我。

1054
00:52:34.860 --> 00:52:35.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1055
00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:36.360
You guys.
你们这些人。

1056
00:52:36.640 --> 00:52:37.140
It worked.
成功了。

1057
00:52:37.660 --> 00:52:38.000
OK.
好吧。

1058
00:52:38.560 --> 00:52:43.820
So now the party is really underway and we see a little bit of a callback to a character
现在派对正式开始了，我们看到了一个对之前角色的致敬片段，

1059
00:52:43.820 --> 00:52:45.960
at 32 minutes, 58 seconds.
在32分58秒处。

1060
00:52:46.160 --> 00:52:48.960
We see Dan Gore, the regional manager.
我们看到了区域经理丹·戈尔。

1061
00:52:49.000 --> 00:52:49.940
He's back.
他又回来了。

1062
00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:54.000
And now we're coming up to the point where Scranton is going to get its shout out.
现在我们要讲到斯克兰顿分公司出镜的时刻了。

1063
00:52:54.360 --> 00:52:54.480
Right.
没错。

1064
00:52:55.300 --> 00:52:55.680
Mm hmm.
嗯哼。

1065
00:52:55.760 --> 00:52:57.120
This is what Michael says.
迈克尔是这么说的。

1066
00:52:57.320 --> 00:53:02.300
He says, hey, I just think you should know one of my salesmen beat your stupid computer.
他说，嘿，我觉得你们应该知道，我手下的一个销售员打败了你们那台蠢电脑。

1067
00:53:02.520 --> 00:53:03.900
So take that asshole.
所以，去你的吧，混蛋。

1068
00:53:03.900 --> 00:53:04.720
Yeah.
耶。

1069
00:53:04.920 --> 00:53:10.160
And then Kelly takes her pizza and smashes it onto Ryan's face on the TV screen.
然后凯莉拿起她的披萨，砸在了电视屏幕上瑞安的脸上。

1070
00:53:10.360 --> 00:53:13.200
That's Scranton's moment in this corporate event.
这就是斯克兰顿在这次公司活动中的高光时刻。

1071
00:53:13.440 --> 00:53:21.060
But wait, then the pizza kid runs up to the webcam and says that he's a minor being held
但等等，接着那个送披萨的孩子跑向摄像头，说他是个未成年人，

1072
00:53:21.060 --> 00:53:22.020
against his will.
正被违背意愿地扣押着。

1073
00:53:22.440 --> 00:53:23.120
Yes.
没错。

1074
00:53:23.380 --> 00:53:26.840
How does anyone in this branch still have a job?
这个分部的人到底是怎么保住工作的？

1075
00:53:27.040 --> 00:53:27.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1076
00:53:28.300 --> 00:53:29.380
I don't know.
我不知道。

1077
00:53:29.760 --> 00:53:36.980
But meanwhile, just as all of this is going on, Andy tries to scratch Angela's back.
但与此同时，就在这一切发生的时候，安迪试图去抓安吉拉的背。

1078
00:53:37.560 --> 00:53:39.600
Andy, what are your moves?
安迪，你到底有什么招数？

1079
00:53:39.600 --> 00:53:44.380
Tell me, what are your moves to like get a lady interested in you?
告诉我，你有什么招数能让女士对你感兴趣？

1080
00:53:44.560 --> 00:53:48.180
First, you have ridiculous pickup lines like the movie in the box.
首先，你用那种荒谬的搭讪台词，比如那个盒子里的电影。

1081
00:53:48.400 --> 00:53:53.380
And then you go up to someone you don't really know and scratch their back.
然后你走到一个不太熟的人面前，去抓人家的背。

1082
00:53:53.380 --> 00:53:54.420
Are you crazy?
你疯了吗？

1083
00:53:55.380 --> 00:53:58.180
Well, she said she had an itch she couldn't reach.
好吧，她说她有个地方痒，自己够不着。

1084
00:53:58.180 --> 00:54:02.100
She did, but I don't think that was an invitation.
她是说了，但我觉得那并不是邀请。

1085
00:54:02.820 --> 00:54:03.020
No.
不是。

1086
00:54:03.460 --> 00:54:05.380
Yeah, that wasn't an invitation, Andy.
没错，那不是邀请，安迪。

1087
00:54:05.560 --> 00:54:09.080
Don't go scratching people's backs unless you're invited to scratch their back.
除非别人邀请你，否则别去抓别人的背。

1088
00:54:09.340 --> 00:54:11.880
And Angela definitely does not seem interested.
而且安吉拉看起来显然一点也不感兴趣。

1089
00:54:12.120 --> 00:54:14.380
And then there's a scene, Jenna, that I love.
然后有一个场景，珍娜，我特别喜欢。

1090
00:54:14.540 --> 00:54:16.380
It's something our show does that I love.
这是我们剧里我非常喜欢的一种处理方式。

1091
00:54:16.520 --> 00:54:17.980
It's never explained.
它从不解释。

1092
00:54:18.200 --> 00:54:21.520
It's just Dwight and Andy standing outside the men's room.
就是德怀特和安迪站在男厕所外面。

1093
00:54:22.140 --> 00:54:24.280
Dwight is clearly on guard.
德怀特显然是在站岗。

1094
00:54:24.360 --> 00:54:24.480
Yeah.
没错。

1095
00:54:24.740 --> 00:54:26.600
By his whole physical posture.
从他整个身体姿态就能看出来。

1096
00:54:26.600 --> 00:54:31.220
So we're just left to assume pizza guys in there on his bathroom break.
所以我们只能假设那个送披萨的在里面上厕所。

1097
00:54:31.380 --> 00:54:32.540
He's been led in there.
他被带进去了。

1098
00:54:32.820 --> 00:54:36.900
And Andy and Dwight have this whole conversation outside the men's room.
然后安迪和德怀特在男厕所外进行了那番对话。

1099
00:54:37.260 --> 00:54:43.940
And at one point, Dwight kicks open the door and says, unless you're going number two,
有一刻，德怀特踢开门说，除非你在上大号，

1100
00:54:44.240 --> 00:54:47.440
you've got about 15 seconds left or something to that effect.
否则你只剩下大约15秒了，大概就是这个意思。

1101
00:54:47.580 --> 00:54:51.900
And I just have to say, I really loved Rain's choice here.
我不得不说，我真的很喜欢雷恩在这里的选择。

1102
00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:54.200
Like the way he kicked the door.
比如他踹门的方式。

1103
00:54:54.420 --> 00:54:55.820
He looked very official.
他看起来非常一本正经。

1104
00:54:55.820 --> 00:54:56.560
He did.
确实。

1105
00:54:56.680 --> 00:55:00.100
And Rain, I feel like his performance in the scene is so great.
而且雷恩，我觉得他在这一幕里的表演太棒了。

1106
00:55:00.360 --> 00:55:01.660
It's all these little moments.
全靠这些小细节。

1107
00:55:01.660 --> 00:55:05.000
He's slightly like pleased, right?
他有点暗自窃喜，对吧？

1108
00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:07.420
That Angela has rejected Andy.
因为安吉拉拒绝了安迪。

1109
00:55:07.640 --> 00:55:09.120
He's still crestfallen.
但他依然很沮丧。

1110
00:55:09.360 --> 00:55:12.280
He's still upset that Andy wants to continue to pursue her.
他还是对安迪想要继续追求安吉拉感到心烦。

1111
00:55:12.420 --> 00:55:14.180
But yet he has a job to do.
但即便如此，他还有工作要做。

1112
00:55:14.320 --> 00:55:16.700
And that is to make sure the pizza guy doesn't escape.
那就是确保送披萨的家伙跑不掉。

1113
00:55:16.700 --> 00:55:26.800
Well, the Dwight character is such a great character because he is so invested and committed to being Michael's number two.
嗯，德怀特这个角色之所以这么棒，是因为他全心全意地致力于成为迈克尔的二把手。

1114
00:55:27.760 --> 00:55:32.580
So much so that in a minute, he's going to be interrogating this pizza kid.
甚至到了下一分钟，他就要去审问这个送披萨的孩子了。

1115
00:55:32.780 --> 00:55:38.080
And Michael is now going to suddenly realize what they've done, that they have kidnapped someone.
而迈克尔现在突然意识到他们做了什么，他们绑架了别人。

1116
00:55:38.080 --> 00:55:40.200
And he starts freaking out.
他开始惊慌失措。

1117
00:55:40.560 --> 00:55:45.440
And it takes Dwight a second because he was so committed to the other choice.
德怀特反应了一会儿，因为他之前太执着于之前的选择了。

1118
00:55:45.640 --> 00:55:48.440
But then he becomes just as committed to the new choice.
但随后他同样全心全意地投入到了新的选择中。

1119
00:55:48.440 --> 00:55:50.120
And he pays for all the pizza.
他还付了所有的披萨钱。

1120
00:55:50.120 --> 00:55:52.560
Yeah, he's so loyal to Michael.
没错，他对迈克尔太忠诚了。

1121
00:55:53.000 --> 00:55:55.640
And it is a little bit like creepy.
这甚至有点让人毛骨悚然。

1122
00:55:55.980 --> 00:55:58.560
It's it reminded me a little bit of like Lord of the Flies.
这让我想起了一点《蝇王》的感觉。

1123
00:55:58.920 --> 00:56:07.100
Like, you know, it's like all of a sudden, you know, when people follow someone who they shouldn't be following.
就像，你知道，当人们盲目追随一个不该追随的人时，突然之间会发生什么。

1124
00:56:07.320 --> 00:56:08.500
And then where does that lead them?
那会把他们引向何方？

1125
00:56:08.560 --> 00:56:09.760
And what are they capable of?
他们又会做出什么事来？

1126
00:56:09.900 --> 00:56:12.360
What was Dwight going to continue to do to this pizza guy?
德怀特原本打算对这个送披萨的人继续做什么？

1127
00:56:12.940 --> 00:56:14.920
Well, it's such a crazy storyline.
嗯，这剧情真是太疯狂了。

1128
00:56:14.920 --> 00:56:20.900
We talked about it, and I feel like so much of it really hinges on Kevin's great performance.
我们讨论过，我觉得这很大程度上取决于凯文出色的表演。

1129
00:56:21.800 --> 00:56:23.040
Yes, I absolutely agree.
是的，我完全同意。

1130
00:56:23.040 --> 00:56:26.180
He was perfect all throughout the scenes.
他在整个场景中的表现都堪称完美。

1131
00:56:26.440 --> 00:56:26.740
Yeah.
没错。

1132
00:56:26.920 --> 00:56:30.580
And we just asked him if he had any memories from his time on the show.
我们问过他，在剧组期间有什么难忘的回忆。

1133
00:56:30.740 --> 00:56:31.740
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的回答。

1134
00:56:32.100 --> 00:56:42.100
My biggest memory or takeaway from the entire experience period was honestly the generosity and the kindness from everybody.
老实说，我整个经历中最深刻的记忆或收获，就是大家表现出的慷慨和友善。

1135
00:56:42.460 --> 00:56:44.380
Everybody went out of their way.
每个人都特别照顾我。

1136
00:56:46.040 --> 00:56:48.760
To accept me, to welcome me with open arMs.
接纳我，张开双臂欢迎我。

1137
00:56:50.140 --> 00:56:54.540
I sat with, you know, a lot of the cast for lunch every day.
我每天午餐都和很多演员坐在一起。

1138
00:56:54.740 --> 00:56:58.080
I think they, you know, I was totally a fish out of water, and I think everybody could see that.
我想他们，你知道，我当时完全是个局外人，我想每个人都看得出来。

1139
00:56:58.400 --> 00:57:02.460
And it's one of those things where you come on set, they welcome you to set in rehearsal, and everybody cheers.
那种感觉就是，当你来到片场，他们在排练时欢迎你，每个人都在欢呼。

1140
00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:06.700
And that is something that I've taken with me.
那是我一直铭记在心的事。

1141
00:57:06.800 --> 00:57:14.100
And I remember going into Glee, how it hit me at some point of like, oh, I'm now in their position as the person who's on this show every week.
我记得后来去拍《欢乐合唱团》时，我突然意识到，哦，我现在处于他们的位置了，成了每周都在剧组里的人。

1142
00:57:14.100 --> 00:57:20.340
And when people come on, I need to treat them how the office people treated me.
当有新人加入时，我需要像《办公室》的伙伴们对待我那样对待他们。

1143
00:57:20.340 --> 00:57:31.900
And whenever I would see people, I'd see Kate, I would see Mindy out at events or whatever it may be, and everyone was just still so nice to me.
每当我见到他们，见到凯特，见到敏迪，在活动或其他场合，每个人对我依然非常友善。

1144
00:57:31.960 --> 00:57:34.880
And they'd come up and be like, oh, I'm so happy.
他们会走过来对我说，哦，我真为你高兴。

1145
00:57:34.880 --> 00:57:37.120
Like, the Glee is doing so well.
《欢乐合唱团》做得真好。

1146
00:57:37.260 --> 00:57:43.040
And it was one of those things where me coming on to a show that was so big, and all these people were so very famous and successful,
当时我加入了一部非常火的剧，而这些人又如此出名且成功，

1147
00:57:43.280 --> 00:57:50.360
that even though I was now on a show that was successful, I still felt very much like the fan.
尽管我现在也身处一部成功的剧里，但我依然感觉自己像个粉丝。

1148
00:57:50.720 --> 00:57:56.740
And the fact that they could come up to me, and they just always treated me with kindness and as an equal.
他们能主动走过来，始终以友善的态度对待我，把我当作平等的人，这一点我永远、永远不会忘记。

1149
00:57:56.740 --> 00:57:59.040
And that's something I will never, ever forget.
这一点我永远、永远不会忘记。

1150
00:57:59.300 --> 00:58:02.780
And I say they, but I realize it's you, you guys.
我说的是“他们”，但我意识到其实就是你们，你们大家。

1151
00:58:03.160 --> 00:58:05.360
So thanks for being so nice.
谢谢你这么客气。

1152
00:58:06.020 --> 00:58:09.680
You know, lady, it's so sweet for him to say that.
你知道吗，女士，他能这么说真是太贴心了。

1153
00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:19.660
And it really takes me back because when I was an aspiring actor and I would get those guest star roles on shows, it would be such a big deal to me.
这真的让我回想起过去，当我还是个怀揣梦想的演员时，能得到那些客串角色的机会，对我来说真的是件大事。

1154
00:58:20.280 --> 00:58:24.620
But I would go on the set, and I would feel just so alone.
但我去片场的时候，总会感到非常孤独。

1155
00:58:25.300 --> 00:58:29.220
And most of the time, people didn't invite me to eat lunch with them.
大多数时候，人们都不会邀请我一起吃午饭。

1156
00:58:29.740 --> 00:58:35.300
And they were in their own world because they had that job every day, so it wasn't particularly special to them.
他们沉浸在自己的世界里，因为他们每天都有那份工作，所以对他们来说这没什么特别的。

1157
00:58:35.580 --> 00:58:40.400
And I would just feel, you know, like I was really on my own.
我当时真的感觉，你知道的，就像我是一个人孤军奋战。

1158
00:58:40.700 --> 00:58:44.500
We've talked about it, like a kid in a new school on the first day of school.
我们聊过这个，就像第一天去新学校的孩子一样。

1159
00:58:44.500 --> 00:58:51.780
Yeah, with all the pressure of, like, the new day and the new place and the new work and all of it.
没错，带着那种压力，比如新的一天、新的环境、新的工作，所有这些加在一起。

1160
00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:57.440
Yeah, and people did not generally go out of their way to try to make me feel better.
是的，而且大家通常也不会特意去想办法让我感觉好受些。

1161
00:58:57.840 --> 00:58:59.160
And that was fine.
那也没关系。

1162
00:58:59.560 --> 00:59:11.100
But I think all of us on The Office had been knocking around for so long and had experienced that feeling so many times that whenever we did have a guest star,
但我认为我们《办公室》剧组的所有人都已经在圈子里摸爬滚打很久了，也经历过很多次那种感觉，所以每当我们有客串演员时，

1163
00:59:11.100 --> 00:59:19.420
I would watch as everyone would go out of their way to introduce themselves, say hello, shake hands, invite that person to eat lunch with them,
我都会看着大家特意去主动做自我介绍、打招呼、握手，邀请那个人一起吃午饭，

1164
00:59:19.900 --> 00:59:21.800
show them where the craft services was.
带他们去看看剧组的餐饮区在哪里。

1165
00:59:22.460 --> 00:59:26.460
I do have this memory of us just being so hospitable.
我确实记得我们当时是多么热情好客。

1166
00:59:26.680 --> 00:59:28.460
It was like, welcome to our house.
就像是，欢迎来到我们的家。

1167
00:59:28.640 --> 00:59:30.460
Let's show you around, give you a tour.
让我们带你四处看看，给你做个向导。

1168
00:59:30.800 --> 00:59:32.140
Do you know where the bathrooms are?
你知道洗手间在哪里吗？

1169
00:59:32.140 --> 00:59:40.480
And I think it was because all of us had been around for so long, experiencing it the other way, that we wanted our show to be different.
我想这是因为我们所有人都已经在圈子里待了很久，经历过那种被冷落的滋味，所以我们希望我们的剧组能有所不同。

1170
00:59:40.780 --> 00:59:41.860
And we just did it.
我们就是这么做了。

1171
00:59:41.900 --> 00:59:43.020
We never talked about it.
我们从来没讨论过这件事。

1172
00:59:43.160 --> 00:59:45.800
It was just this collective thing that we all did.
这只是我们大家共同做的一件事。

1173
00:59:46.540 --> 00:59:46.760
Yeah.
没错。

1174
00:59:47.120 --> 00:59:57.880
And you definitely remember with each job, especially when you're starting out, if there was one person that showed you kindness, you just like remember it and you hold on to it.
你肯定记得每一份工作，尤其是刚起步的时候，如果有一个人对你表现出善意，你真的会记住并铭记在心。

1175
00:59:57.880 --> 01:00:06.960
And, and I'm so glad that our show was like that for Kevin, you know, and that he took that same philosophy to glee with him.
而且，我很高兴我们的剧组对凯文来说就是那样，他也把同样的理念带到了《欢乐合唱团》。

1176
01:00:07.580 --> 01:00:09.160
Yeah, that's really cool.
是的，那真的很棒。

1177
01:00:09.340 --> 01:00:20.300
Well, we also asked him if he, after all this time, still gets recognized as the pizza guy from The Office, even though he's gone on to all these other amazing projects.
嗯，我们还问过他，时隔这么久，尽管他后来参与了那么多精彩的项目，但他是否还会被认作是《办公室》里的那个披萨小哥。

1178
