01:07:59.090 --> 01:08:01.990
I don't know if I just miss Ed a lot.
我不知道是因为我太想念埃德了，

1319
01:08:02.110 --> 01:08:04.510
And he's so charming in this scene.
还是因为他在这一幕里太有魅力了。

1320
01:08:04.690 --> 01:08:04.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1321
01:08:05.090 --> 01:08:07.050
Or if it's just the time we're in.
又或者是受我们现在所处时期的影响。

1322
01:08:08.570 --> 01:08:09.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

1323
01:08:09.590 --> 01:08:14.330
I've also just fallen in love with Andy during this rewatch.
这次重温，我还爱上了安迪这个角色。

1324
01:08:14.710 --> 01:08:19.890
You know, we've talked about how I have this new appreciation for Ryan.
你知道，我们聊过我对瑞安有了新的欣赏。

1325
01:08:20.130 --> 01:08:20.590
Right.
没错。

1326
01:08:20.750 --> 01:08:25.250
But I also just have been loving the character of Andy and his journey.
但我最近也一直很喜欢安迪这个角色以及他的成长历程。

1327
01:08:26.710 --> 01:08:28.150
But I don't know, Angela.
但我不知道，安吉拉。

1328
01:08:28.330 --> 01:08:34.210
I also have to say, I know I mentioned that the weight of my heart is to put together a grill and break down the box.
我还要说，虽然我提过我心里的重担是组装烤架和拆掉包装盒。

1329
01:08:34.210 --> 01:08:44.850
But I think that if there was a guy that I actually was not that interested in, if he did this, I would be like, OK, all right.
但我觉得，如果是一个我本来没那么感兴趣的男生，他要是做了这种事，我也会觉得，好吧，行吧。

1330
01:08:46.210 --> 01:08:47.950
It is so sweet.
这太贴心了。

1331
01:08:48.290 --> 01:08:50.070
It's so, so charming.
真的非常、非常有魅力。

1332
01:08:50.510 --> 01:08:55.370
You know, my husband is a really good singer and he doesn't really sing around people.
你知道，我丈夫唱歌很好听，但他平时不太会在别人面前唱。

1333
01:08:55.730 --> 01:09:02.030
But when we first started dating, we went out and there was karaoke and I didn't really know the side of him.
但我们刚开始约会时，有次出去唱卡拉OK，我之前真的没见过他那一面。

1334
01:09:02.190 --> 01:09:03.370
He's like an acapella guy.
他是个阿卡贝拉爱好者。

1335
01:09:03.370 --> 01:09:08.890
And he got up and sang Journey and he brought down the bar.
他上台唱了Journey乐队的歌，简直把全场都震住了。

1336
01:09:09.050 --> 01:09:11.310
And I was like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

1337
01:09:13.970 --> 01:09:17.650
But it was just so, so sweet in this moment.
这一刻真的太、太贴心了。

1338
01:09:17.870 --> 01:09:20.750
Andy, you know, and Andy will go on to sing to Angela again.
安迪，你知道，安迪之后还会再为安吉拉唱歌。

1339
01:09:21.270 --> 01:09:26.030
But, you know, he must really like her if he's going to bust out the acapella group.
但你要知道，如果他愿意把阿卡贝拉组合都搬出来，那他一定真的很喜欢她。

1340
01:09:26.650 --> 01:09:28.190
Yeah, he's all in.
没错，他全情投入了。

1341
01:09:29.090 --> 01:09:31.670
I hope one of those guys was Broccoli Rob.
我希望其中一个人是西兰花罗布。

1342
01:09:31.930 --> 01:09:33.250
Oh, it had to have been.
哦，那肯定是他。

1343
01:09:33.370 --> 01:09:33.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1344
01:09:34.250 --> 01:09:39.350
And Angela just looks at him and says she has to go clean up the party.
而安吉拉只是看着他，说她得去清理派对现场。

1345
01:09:39.570 --> 01:09:44.150
And then we reveal that the whole bullpen has watched this.
然后我们发现整个办公区的人都看到了这一幕。

1346
01:09:44.650 --> 01:09:44.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1347
01:09:45.550 --> 01:09:46.470
Including Dwight.
包括德怀特。

1348
01:09:47.370 --> 01:09:47.690
Yeah.
没错。

1349
01:09:47.690 --> 01:09:54.390
And before we move on, Jenna, 38 minutes, 15 seconds.
在我们继续之前，珍娜，38分15秒。

1350
01:09:55.350 --> 01:09:57.170
Prime elbow poof.
绝佳的肘部蓬松效果。

1351
01:09:58.070 --> 01:10:00.330
Prime elbow poof of the sweater.
毛衣肘部那块蓬松得简直绝了。

1352
01:10:00.610 --> 01:10:03.150
I don't even understand this sweater, you guys.
伙计们，我甚至都看不懂这件毛衣。

1353
01:10:03.350 --> 01:10:10.570
It was skinny at the top, then had a big floofy poofy part right at the elbow, then skinny again down to the wriSt.
它上部很紧身，肘部那儿却突然变得又大又蓬，到了手腕又变回紧身了。

1354
01:10:10.570 --> 01:10:14.490
And it also had lace sewn into the v-neck.
而且V领处还缝了蕾丝。

1355
01:10:15.930 --> 01:10:27.870
Yeah, I mean, I think that we have to acknowledge that Andy serenaded Angela while she was wearing this terrible blouse.
没错，我觉得我们必须承认，安迪给安吉拉唱小夜曲时，她穿的就是这件糟糕的衬衫。

1356
01:10:29.050 --> 01:10:33.030
No other man was going to hit on Angela today.
今天根本不会有别的男人去搭讪安吉拉。

1357
01:10:33.190 --> 01:10:33.590
Well.
嗯。

1358
01:10:33.770 --> 01:10:37.550
I'll tell you that because that blouse is a repellent.
我敢这么说，因为那件衬衫简直就是驱蚊剂。

1359
01:10:38.110 --> 01:10:43.370
I think we have a callback to a flirty shade of beige here.
我觉得这里又呼应了那种撩人的米色。

1360
01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:44.090
Yes.
没错。

1361
01:10:44.230 --> 01:10:46.230
Very flirty shade of beige again.
又是那种非常撩人的米色。

1362
01:10:46.230 --> 01:10:46.790
Yes.
是的。

1363
01:10:46.990 --> 01:10:51.530
Well, actually, it's like a Victorian shade of beige with the poofy sleeve, right?
其实，配上那蓬蓬袖，这更像是维多利亚风格的米色，对吧？

1364
01:10:52.130 --> 01:10:52.390
Yeah.
没错。

1365
01:10:52.670 --> 01:10:53.450
The poofy elbow.
那蓬蓬的肘部。

1366
01:10:53.450 --> 01:10:58.690
So, Dwight ogles her in this flirty shade of beige, and Andy sings to her.
所以，德怀特盯着穿这身撩人米色的她看，而安迪则为她唱歌。

1367
01:10:58.870 --> 01:11:00.810
So, clearly, something was working.
显然，这招奏效了。

1368
01:11:02.010 --> 01:11:03.270
It's a shocker.
真是令人震惊。

1369
01:11:05.630 --> 01:11:12.810
Well, now we go into Michael's office, and he and Dwight are just both miserable over this day.
好了，现在镜头转到迈克尔的办公室，他和德怀特对这一天感到无比痛苦。

1370
01:11:13.370 --> 01:11:15.030
Yeah, they've had a day.
是啊，他们真是度过了糟糕的一天。

1371
01:11:15.550 --> 01:11:22.570
And Michael says, more than anything, he's bummed that he did not get to have authentic New York sushi.
迈克尔说，最让他难过的是，他没能吃到正宗的纽约寿司。

1372
01:11:22.830 --> 01:11:23.590
Not a thing.
根本没吃到。

1373
01:11:23.970 --> 01:11:24.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1374
01:11:24.310 --> 01:11:26.430
New York has very good sushi.
纽约的寿司确实很棒。

1375
01:11:26.730 --> 01:11:27.030
Yeah.
没错。

1376
01:11:27.130 --> 01:11:29.930
But it is certainly, I don't think, the sushi capital.
但我不认为那里是寿司之都。

1377
01:11:30.970 --> 01:11:33.750
But whatever, Michael is really, really bummed.
不过无所谓，迈克尔真的很沮丧。

1378
01:11:34.070 --> 01:11:34.630
Yeah.
是啊。

1379
01:11:34.750 --> 01:11:40.130
And he says to Dwight, I think we should go to New York and get that sushi.
他对德怀特说，我觉得我们应该去纽约吃那顿寿司。

1380
01:11:40.870 --> 01:11:41.790
You're driving.
你来开车。

1381
01:11:42.750 --> 01:11:44.150
Dwight is so excited.
德怀特兴奋极了。

1382
01:11:44.370 --> 01:11:45.590
He can't wait.
他等不及了。

1383
01:11:45.870 --> 01:11:50.610
He can't wait to drive all the way to New York to crash the tail end of this corporate party
他迫不及待地想开车一路赶到纽约，去搅合公司派对的尾声，

1384
01:11:50.610 --> 01:11:53.710
and get the leftover sushi that no one else wanted to eat.
然后去吃那些没人想吃的剩寿司。

1385
01:11:54.290 --> 01:11:55.990
That's been sitting out for a while.
那些已经放了很久的寿司。

1386
01:11:55.990 --> 01:11:57.250
For a long while.
放了很久很久。

1387
01:11:57.670 --> 01:11:58.930
I just want to say.
我只想说。

1388
01:11:59.210 --> 01:11:59.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1389
01:12:00.070 --> 01:12:01.330
So that's what they do.
于是他们就这么做了。

1390
01:12:01.510 --> 01:12:02.150
They get there.
他们到了那里。

1391
01:12:02.350 --> 01:12:03.390
They go into the party.
他们走进派对现场。

1392
01:12:03.710 --> 01:12:05.870
They get kicked out pretty much immediately.
结果几乎立刻就被赶了出来。

1393
01:12:05.870 --> 01:12:06.910
There's no one there.
那里已经没人了。

1394
01:12:07.110 --> 01:12:08.890
But they grab a plate of sushi.
但他们还是抓了一盘寿司。

1395
01:12:08.890 --> 01:12:12.130
And then they go and they sit on the hood of Dwight's car.
然后他们跑去坐在德怀特的车盖上。

1396
01:12:12.710 --> 01:12:15.890
And guys, this, they did not go to New York to shoot this.
伙计们，这一幕，他们可不是去纽约拍的。

1397
01:12:16.050 --> 01:12:21.410
Obviously, this is a little parking lot that they found in downtown LA, I believe.
显然，这只是他们在洛杉矶市中心找的一个小停车场，我想是这样。

1398
01:12:21.410 --> 01:12:24.390
I recognized it because I think I've shot there.
我认出来了，因为我觉得我也在那里拍过戏。

1399
01:12:24.810 --> 01:12:25.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1400
01:12:25.170 --> 01:12:29.090
They are just eating the sushi and they are making fun of Ryan.
他们就在那儿吃着寿司，还一边嘲笑瑞安。

1401
01:12:30.270 --> 01:12:36.250
And someone leaves the party and says to Michael, hey, that was pretty awesome, you know, when
有人离开派对对迈克尔说，嘿，那真是太棒了，你知道，当

1402
01:12:36.250 --> 01:12:37.690
you called Ryan out like that.
你那样当众指责瑞安的时候。

1403
01:12:37.890 --> 01:12:40.990
And it is, it's like all he needed, right?
就是这样，这正是他所需要的，对吧？

1404
01:12:41.090 --> 01:12:41.230
Yeah.
没错。

1405
01:12:41.310 --> 01:12:42.430
He feels seen.
他感觉自己被关注到了。

1406
01:12:42.770 --> 01:12:44.170
And they're having sushi.
他们正在吃寿司。

1407
01:12:44.170 --> 01:12:45.430
And they're in New York.
他们身处纽约。

1408
01:12:45.430 --> 01:12:46.830
And now he can go home.
现在他可以回家了。

1409
01:12:47.190 --> 01:12:47.670
Yeah.
没错。

1410
01:12:47.670 --> 01:12:55.030
He sets the tray of sushi and soy sauce on someone else's car and they go home.
他把寿司和酱油托盘放在别人的车上，然后他们就回家了。

1411
01:12:56.290 --> 01:12:57.570
It's pretty amazing.
真是太神奇了。

1412
01:12:57.910 --> 01:12:59.970
And then we have just a little tag at the end.
然后我们在结尾还有一个小彩蛋。

1413
01:13:00.250 --> 01:13:07.750
We just see Ryan in full douche mode, winking at the camera from his New York party that's
我们看到瑞安完全是一副混蛋样，在纽约派对上对着镜头眨眼，派对

1414
01:13:07.750 --> 01:13:08.630
in full swing.
正进行得如火如荼。

1415
01:13:08.790 --> 01:13:09.310
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1416
01:13:09.450 --> 01:13:10.910
So pleased with himself.
对自己非常满意。

1417
01:13:11.310 --> 01:13:15.730
Well, I don't know if you thought about it, but the scene had basically three couples
嗯，我不知道你们有没有注意到，但那个场景里基本上有三对情侣

1418
01:13:15.730 --> 01:13:17.990
in it, having intimate moments.
在享受亲密时刻。

1419
01:13:18.250 --> 01:13:21.070
We have Jim and Pam dinner on the roof.
吉姆和帕姆在屋顶吃晚餐。

1420
01:13:21.250 --> 01:13:24.950
We have Andy and Angela serenading and accounting.
安迪和安吉拉在唱歌和算账。

1421
01:13:25.170 --> 01:13:28.750
And we have Michael and Dwight having dinner in a parking lot.
还有迈克尔和德怀特在停车场吃晚餐。

1422
01:13:29.310 --> 01:13:29.870
Yeah.
没错。

1423
01:13:31.310 --> 01:13:32.390
Very sweet.
非常甜蜜。

1424
01:13:32.670 --> 01:13:33.550
Very sweet.
非常甜蜜。

1425
01:13:33.930 --> 01:13:36.970
And we had one hostage, but we let him go.
我们还有一个“人质”，但我们把他放了。

1426
01:13:39.710 --> 01:13:44.110
Well, guys, that was lunch party part two.
好了，伙计们，这就是午餐派对的第二部分。

1427
01:13:44.110 --> 01:13:50.150
And a big thank you to Jen Salata and Kevin McHale and Steve Ducharer for all the behind
非常感谢简·萨拉塔、凯文·麦克海尔和史蒂夫·杜查雷尔提供的所有幕后

1428
01:13:50.150 --> 01:13:51.210
the scenes details.
细节。

1429
01:13:51.590 --> 01:13:56.790
Yeah, guys, thank you so much for always letting us reach out to get those details each week.
是的，伙计们，非常感谢你们每周都让我们联系并获取这些细节。

1430
01:13:56.930 --> 01:13:58.270
We really appreciate it.
我们真的很感激。

1431
01:13:58.350 --> 01:14:01.470
And we're going to be doing it for like three more years.
我们还要再做三年左右。

1432
01:14:01.710 --> 01:14:03.150
So don't get tired of us.
所以别对我们感到厌烦。

1433
01:14:03.490 --> 01:14:04.870
Everyone, check your DMs.
大家，检查一下你们的私信。

1434
01:14:04.950 --> 01:14:07.830
If you've ever had anything to do with the office, please check in.
如果你曾经和《办公室》有过任何交集，请联系我们。

1435
01:14:08.010 --> 01:14:08.830
We'll be there.
我们会回复的。

1436
01:14:08.970 --> 01:14:12.150
There's a good chance Jen and I are there saying, hey, what's up?
很有可能我和简会出现在那里说，嘿，最近怎么样？

1437
01:14:13.530 --> 01:14:15.350
All right, guys, we'll see you next week.
好了，伙计们，我们下周见。

1438
01:14:15.590 --> 01:14:16.090
Take care.
保重。

